  "articleBody": "Ever wonder why your kitchen just doesn't feel right, even after a remodel? Often, it comes down to appliance layout. Many folks focus on aesthetics but forget the flow. For example, if your fridge is far from your prep area or your dishwasher door blocks a main pathway, you're going to feel it every day. You've got to think about how you actually cook and move around the space. Are multiple people cooking at once? Do you need a landing spot right next to the microwave? These are crucial questions. We always look at things like door swings, clearance around appliances, and how much counter space you need for specific tasks. Ignoring these practicalities can lead to a beautiful kitchen that's a pain to use. Sometimes, just shifting an appliance by a few inches can make a world of difference in your daily routine. If you're constantly bumping into things or taking extra steps, it might be time to rethink your kitchen's organization. Getting the layout right from the start means a much more enjoyable and functional space.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}